WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.250
Friendship

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:22.360
thief

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:22.360
parent and child crooks

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.050
<b>Episode 2: You Have a Lot to Say to Me, Don't You?</b>

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.780
<b>Episode 2: You Have a Lot to Say to Me, Don't You?</b>

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:36.190
Shibe! You have the hots 
for Sawaragi, right?

00:01:36.190 --> 00:01:37.770
Do you want to know?

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.620
Hey, Sawaragi, your face is bright red!

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:46.620
Hmm? How about you, Tenji?

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:49.710
Do you want me to tell you?

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:56.470
Fine, but only if you ask out loud 
and say, "Tell me, please."

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:02.220
As if. There's no way you'd say it,

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:07.230
<b>- You may only speak when reading a question.
 (If you break this rule, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:06.800
'cause if you did, the debt you worked 
so hard to lower would all come back.

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.790
I can see right through you.

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:14.250
One of you is trying to dump 
the debt all on Kokorogi.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:20.570
But that won't work. Since I talked, 
my debt is now doubled.

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:24.950
Basically, I'm the one with 
the most debt now, no question.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.950
Katagiri Yuichi

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:32.300
And if this is game over, the traitor's
 gonna be the big loser, here.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:36.410
It was written on my question card.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:42.390
"Rule change: The last place penalty will go 
to the person with the least debt."

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:42.390
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:42.390
<b></b>Rule change: The last place penalty will go to the person with the least debt.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:43.910
Huh? No way!

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.220
Of course he's bluffing.

00:02:45.220 --> 00:02:48.320
Oh, right! Nobody would believe that.

00:02:48.320 --> 00:02:49.850
Are you sure about that?

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:53.610
Imagine you're the traitor. 
Think about it carefully.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:58.870
You've succeeded in reducing 
your debt and are poised to win.

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:01.990
Now you just have to aim 
the last place penalty at your target.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:04.410
It makes you feel just like a hunter.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:09.080
But what if, at the moment 
you're about to pull the trigger,

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:13.290
you learn told that <i>you</i> were 
the one being hunted?

00:03:15.890 --> 00:03:19.400
You mustn't speak. If you do, 
you'll be hunted down.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.490
Caught in Katagiri Yuichi's trap, speaking out

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:26.460
would be the same as confessing 
that you have the least debt.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:29.620
So, you cannot speak. You cannot move.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.190
You have to wait in silence.

00:03:32.190 --> 00:03:35.360
As if! It's a joke! Just a joke.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:37.780
I only wanted to change the mood.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:41.990
There's no traitor here. I trust all of you.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.370
<b>Class Lesson
 When You See a Stranger, Expect a Thief</b>

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.370
Okay, let's get back to the game.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:49.750
I think the question was, 
"Will we always be friends?"

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:55.010
It's a no-brainer. 
The answer is obviously "yes."

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:56.140
Right?

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:59.760
That look... it's his final warning.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:04.730
Let's make this a "yes." Otherwise 
the traitor will be the one who dies.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:08.720
It'll be fun to see if the traitor 
falls for his bluff or not!

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.220
I'm so excited!

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:20.940
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, if you are present,
 please tell us the answer.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:26.570
Kokkuri-san, Kokkuri-san, 
if you are present, tell us the answer.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:32.040
<b>Yes</b>

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:34.040
Yes! Correct answer!

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:36.920
You've cleared the Kokkuri-san game!

00:04:37.890 --> 00:04:39.770
Oh, my God!

00:04:39.770 --> 00:04:41.710
With wit and courage like that,

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:44.800
he doesn't seem like 
an ordinary high schooler.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:48.510
However, he paid quite a price 
to clear the game.

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:51.070
Suspicion really does beget monsters.

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:54.140
In order to clear the game,

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:59.370
Katagiri Yuichi planted the seed of doubt 
that one of them is a traitor.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.280
<b>Group C 
First Game: Kokkuri-san Game</b>

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:05.280
<b>CLEARED</b>

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.280
<b>Prize won: Two million yen</b>

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:09.270
<i>I have to uncover the traitor 
before the second game.</i>

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:11.540
<i>And to do that...</i>

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.040
Guys, how much debt do you have now?

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.330
We should all have the same amount.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:22.340
<b><u>Mikasa Tenji</u> 
Debt: 3.6 million yen
 (self-reported)</b>

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:22.570
The first game took 400,000 off our 
4 million debt, so it's 3.6 million now.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.800
<b><u>Mikasa Tenji</u> 
Debt: 3.6 million yen
 (self-reported)</b>

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.800
<b><u>Shibe Makoto</u> 
 3.6 million yen
 (self-reported)</b>

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.800
<b><u>Sawaragi Shiho </u> 
Debt: 3.6 million yen 
 (self-reported)</b>

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:27.800
<b><u>Kokorogi Yutori</u>
 Debt: 3.6 million yen 
 (self-reported)</b>

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.660
M-Me too, of course.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:27.140
I haven't lost more than anyone else.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.430
Mikasa Tenji

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.430
Should we show the back of our name tags?

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.310
Not a chance. Your debt would double.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.000
But you already have...

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.060
...because you just talked.

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.690
No, I'm at 3.6 million, too.

00:05:42.170 --> 00:05:46.990
It did double when I talked, 
but I'd already cut it in half,

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.990
If the 10 yen coin goes to "yes," you clear the game. 
If the 10 yen coin goes to "no," only the reader's debt will be halved.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.860
Friendship

00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.860
so it ended up even.

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:51.740
<b>- Manabu-kun selects a question reader. 
- The reader opens a numbered envelope.
- If you win, you get two million yen.
- Everyone's debt will go down 400,000 at a time.
- You may only speak when reading a question. 
(If you break this rule, your debt is doubled.)</b>

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:54.720
In the first game, I bet our answers 
didn't match because we were nervous.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:57.710
Let's start over fresh in the second 
game and trust each other.

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.730
Hey, are you done? You talk too much.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.090
Uh... yeah.

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:04.290
Okay, let's go, then!

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.090
Oh, sorry. My shoelace.

00:06:07.690 --> 00:06:11.120
Huh? We'll go without you.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.600
Yeah, I'll catch up in a sec.

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:20.770
<i>Everyone has the same debt? 
Sorry, but I can't believe that.</i>

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.270
Oh, he noticed!

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:25.360
Yes.

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:30.030
The question cards are the only things 
that show the conditions for reducing debt.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.030
If you check those, you'll understand 
how the amounts changed in the game.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.560
If the 10 yen coin goes to "no," only the reader's debt will be halved.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.870
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:37.870
If the 10 yen coin goes to "yes," you clear the game.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.870
The text is disappearing!

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:42.610
Too bad. We used a special 
ink for certain parts,

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.380
so the text would disappear 
after a fixed amount of time.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Reader chooses the question.</b>

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:45.380
<b>Question:
 "Will we always be friends?"</b>

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.420
Damn!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:48.090
Katagiri Yuichi

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:48.500
Yuichi?

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:53.890
What's wrong? You look upset.

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.850
O-Oh, it's nothing. What's up, Sawaragi?

00:06:57.850 --> 00:07:00.230
I wanted to talk to you alone.

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.680
What do you think about
 this situation, Yuichi?

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:09.990
Do you really think one of us is a traitor?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.130
I think so.

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:17.180
You agree, right?

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:19.680
If you know who the traitor is, tell me!

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:23.430
At least tell me who you suspect!

00:07:23.430 --> 00:07:28.130
The one I suspect the most is you, Sawaragi.

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:32.100
No way! Why me?!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:34.640
Before the game started, you said...

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:40.310
Given the circumstances, I don't think we 
should try and figure out whose debt it is.

00:07:40.830 --> 00:07:43.420
The Sawaragi Shiho I know

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:48.900
would never forgive the thief who stole the
 school trip fund and put us in this game.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.900
Especially if it was a friend.

00:07:52.570 --> 00:07:56.740
Sorry, Yuichi. I have to 
apologize about something.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:02.250
I thought you were the one 
who stole the money.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.620
Huh?!

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:07.690
B-Because I'm poor?

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:10.640
You pitied me because I'm poor 
and my parents are gone?

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:12.410
That's why you didn't question me?

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:14.650
No! It wasn't that at all!

00:08:14.650 --> 00:08:16.510
What other reason is there, then?!

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.040
I-It's...

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:19.140
What is it?!

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:23.350
It's because... I like you, Yuichi.

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.230
Eh?

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.440
Huh?!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:29.360
It isn't pity or anything.

00:08:29.690 --> 00:08:33.020
It's because I like you, Yuichi. So...

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:35.700
It's okay. I get it. I get it now.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:38.200
<b>Friendship</b>

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.820
So, do you still suspect me?

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:44.830
Nope. You aren't the thief, Yuichi.

00:08:44.830 --> 00:08:47.210
But I have to apologize 
about one more thing.

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:52.620
Actually, my debt right now 
isn't 3.6 million.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.510
It's 7.6 million.

00:08:56.730 --> 00:08:59.470
<i>Her debt should be half, but it's double?!</i>

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.470
<b>4 million yen x 2 - 400,000 yen</b>

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.470
<b>7.6 million yen</b>

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:03.020
Remember when I almost yelled?

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.960
I guess I made a little sound.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:12.280
And you were so surprised, 
you lied about it?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.320
Mm-hmm.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:18.490
In that fifth question, I think you 
were trying to protect Yutori,

00:09:18.490 --> 00:09:22.150
but the one you really protected was me.

00:09:24.220 --> 00:09:28.390
Yuichi, I won't betray you, no matter what.

00:09:28.390 --> 00:09:31.000
I'll believe you, no matter what.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.210
Let's beat the Tomodachi Game together.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:37.550
All right. Let's cooperate.

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:39.470
Katagiri Yuichi.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:42.810
When money's involved, he becomes 
a sharp judge of character,

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.820
but that isn't enough to 
win the Tomodachi Game.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:52.480
Because there are still others willing 
to destroy that friendship.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.920
W-Where are we?

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:05.410
The roof? I thought we were indoors.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.250
All righty, everyone!

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:13.840
Huh? Manabu-kun?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.760
You gotta call me Manabu-sensei 
now, you dumbass.

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.640
All right, listen up!

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:26.880
You're keeping secrets 
from each other, aren't you?

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:29.560
Today, I want you to spill all the beans!

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:35.920
The gods are also watching over you 
from up in the big, blue sky.

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.490
<b>Go four-eyes!</b>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>*clap clap clap*</b>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>that hair lol</b>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>she's cute</b>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>hi</b>

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>hair lol</b>

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:37.900
<b>yo</b>

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>i was waiting!</b>

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>oh lol they started lol</b>

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.530
<b>did they finally start</b>

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>*clap*</b>

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>hi im god</b>

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>god</b>

00:10:38.400 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>*clap*</b>

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:38.740
<b>wait</b>

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.950
Let's get started!

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:45.450
The second game is Bad-Mouth Sugoroku!

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>*clap*</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>i'm so excited</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>first stream</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>*clap*</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>hype</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>good morning</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>hi</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>heyo</b>

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:49.830
<b>*clap*</b>

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:52.130
Sugoroku? So these are spaces?

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:56.080
In Bad-Mouth Sugoroku, you win
 by taking your friends out

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:57.800
and sending them straight to hell.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.880
Send our friends to hell?

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.970
Yeah. Otherwise, it's just normal Sugoroku.

00:11:02.970 --> 00:11:06.680
Those are the detailed rules. 
Read them carefully!

00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:06.680
<b>- The game is played in periods 
- Each period, you bad-mouth someone 
- Write it down on the bad-mouth card in the private room 
- Once you enter the private room, you can't leave for three minutes 
- You can write as many things as you want about each person 
- You may submit a blank bad-mouth card 
- You may lie (if the lie is revealed, you'll be forced back to the start) 
- The number of spaces you move is determined by the god survey</b>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:08.990
I don't get it at all.

00:11:08.990 --> 00:11:11.100
All right, want to try it out, then?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:13.110
<b>Tomodachi Game</b>

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.480
<b>Bad-Mouth</b>

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:17.120
You go into the private room one at a time 
and write trash about someone.

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.110
<b>Bad-Mouth</b>

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:21.820
Bad-mouth someone on a bad-mouth card,
 then put it in the box.

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:25.030
<b>Bad-Mouth 
Box</b>

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:27.270
I'll collect the cards from the box 
and then read them.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:28.500
<b>Bad-Mouth</b>

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:28.500
<b>Bad-Mouth 
Reading</b>

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:28.500
Ta-da!

00:11:28.800 --> 00:11:31.580
"Kokorogi Yutori is actually a G cup."

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:34.420
"Shibe Makoto wears a wig."

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.000
Hey! That's not true!

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:38.810
"Sawaragi Shiho has athlete's foot."

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:42.810
"Mikasa Tenji wears fake 
glasses just for the looks."

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:46.420
"Katagiri Yuichi is actually rich."

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:51.270
<b>A. Shibe Makoto — wig 
B. Sawaragi Shiho — athlete's foot
 C. Katagiri Yuichi — rich
 D. Kokorogi Yutori — G cup
 E. Mikasa Tenji — fake glasses</b>

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:53.070
Once everyone's bad-mouthing is read, 
we do a survey with the gods,

00:11:52.890 --> 00:11:54.730
<b><b>The Customer Is God</b></b>

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:55.720
the viewers funding the Tomodachi Game.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:56.620
Viewers?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>hmm</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>calm down! this isn't the time to worry</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>a wig at that age is wigcked</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>fake glasses should apologize to the tryhards</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>a wig is unforgivable but I can relate</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>Yutori-chan is so cute</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>the rich guy is unforgivable!</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>that's tough</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>I'm watching</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>athlete's foot? I feel bad for her</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>will someone pick Shibe?</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>none of them are really unforgivable</b>

00:11:56.150 --> 00:12:00.570
<b>im a god</b>

00:11:56.620 --> 00:11:58.390
Are we being turned into a show?

00:11:58.390 --> 00:12:00.970
And the survey says...

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:00.930
<b>Tallying results...</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Q: Who is the most "unforgivable"?</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Shibe Makoto</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Sawaragi Shiho</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Katagiri Yuichi</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Kokorogi Yutori</b>

00:11:58.590 --> 00:12:01.920
<b>Mikasa Tenji</b>

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.660
<b>Shibe Makoto — move 5 spaces</b>

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.660
<b>Katagiri Yuichi — move 4 spaces</b>

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.660
<b>Sawaragi Shiho — move 3 spaces</b>

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.660
<b>Mikasa Tenji — move 2 spaces</b>

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.660
<b>Kokorogi Yutori — move 1 space</b>

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:06.090
That's how we decide 
how many spaces you move.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:06.830
<b>Start</b>

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:10.620
You move the number of spaces you get 
and then follow the instructions.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:16.620
So, the survey determines popularity 
and unpopular people score higher?

00:12:16.620 --> 00:12:22.050
Yeah, but the first person to reach 
the goal will suffer a massive loss.

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:23.630
What's that supposed to mean?

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:27.170
When at least one person reaches 
the goal, you clear the game.

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:30.200
Each person will get a 400,000 yen reward.

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.970
<b>400,000 yen per person</b>

00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:32.730
But anyone left on the board 
when the game ends

00:12:32.270 --> 00:12:33.260
<b>Additional Debt</b>

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.270
gets an additional one million in debt.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.310
<b>1 Million Yen!!</b>

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:40.320
They won't have to play the third game, 
and they can go home for a while.

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.320
<b>Go home!!</b>

00:12:41.150 --> 00:12:42.900
W-We can go home!

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:46.620
Spill all your friends' secrets 
and keep bad-mouthing them

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:49.920
until someone falls into 
that hell of a goal.

00:12:49.920 --> 00:12:52.870
And that's Bad-Mouth Sugoroku! 
Doesn't it sound fun?

00:12:52.870 --> 00:12:56.460
It doesn't sound fun at all! 
There's no way we can do that!

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.960
Just turn in a blank card, then.

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.920
<b>You may submit a blank bad-mouth card</b>

00:13:01.120 --> 00:13:04.620
But what if everyone's 
bad-mouth card is blank?

00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:09.690
Then we don't survey the gods, 
and everyone moves one space.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:14.100
Okay, so if nobody writes anything, 
we'll all reach the goal together.

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.640
Yeah. But then you just get 
a two million yen reward,

00:13:17.640 --> 00:13:19.980
and everyone will be forced 
to play the third game.

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>exciting</b>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>forced to play</b>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>u mad?</b>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>Shiho-samaaa</b>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>you'd better listen up</b>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.400
That isn't a problem at all.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:24.910
Oh? But if one person betrays you,

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:28.110
everyone who left it blank will be 
at a huge disadvantage.

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.980
Sawaragi, don't worry.

00:13:30.980 --> 00:13:33.460
We're friends. We won't betray each other.

00:13:33.460 --> 00:13:34.730
Yuichi...

00:13:39.770 --> 00:13:42.350
That's right! We're besties!

00:13:42.350 --> 00:13:45.340
Let's all reach the goal together, guys.

00:13:45.340 --> 00:13:48.300
That's the only way 
to protect our friendship.

00:13:49.900 --> 00:13:51.810
Yeah, let's all reach the goal together!

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:55.650
It's just like a marathon.

00:13:55.650 --> 00:13:58.920
But no one's ever running 
all together at the end.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:14:02.290
That's true. Humans are very
 calculating creatures.

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:07.530
I wonder how many spaces they'll last 
together if it only disadvantages them.

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:09.530
<b>First Period</b>

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:12.280
Okay. The first submissions 
have been collected.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:16.960
And... zero bad-mouthing! 
They were all blank cards.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:20.120
So, everyone move one space 
together like friends.

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.590
<b>Players who stop on this space will 
"Lose your wallet on the way home from school"</b>

00:14:24.960 --> 00:14:26.590
<b>- 100,000 yen</b>

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:28.840
Minus 100,000 yen?

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:31.080
No way! You didn't tell us about that!

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:35.270
Huh? Sure I did. I said it was 
normal Sugoroku otherwise.

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:33.680
<b>friendly 100,000 lol</b>

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:34.640
<b>Shibe-kyun</b>

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>-100,000</b>

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.270
<b>lolol</b>

00:14:35.270 --> 00:14:41.290
If we get 100,000 more debt per space, 
we'll end up with six million yen!

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.270
<b>Second Period</b>

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:46.190
The second round of cards 
were all blank, too.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:48.790
Okay, everyone, move forward one space.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.570
<b>Players who stop on this space will 
"Buy a painting of a dolphin from 
a beautiful woman on the street"</b>

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.570
<b>- 500,000 yen</b>

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:54.220
F-Five hundred thousand?

00:14:54.220 --> 00:14:56.950
Why would they all be one hundred?

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:00.830
Oh, dear. You look a little pale, guys.

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:04.670
I guess you did just add 
600,000 of debt in two moves.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:07.560
I've got some great advice for you, though!

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:08.970
<b>All of the debt added during the game</b>

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:08.970
<b>will be given to whoever reaches the goal first.</b>

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:12.200
Yup! Right now, with 600,000 
each from five people,

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:14.970
you can add three million 
to someone else's debt!

00:15:14.970 --> 00:15:18.730
Now do you see why it's stupid 
for you to finish together?

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:20.730
Don't let him manipulate us!

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.250
Yeah, we get it, Shiho.

00:15:23.250 --> 00:15:24.900
Thanks, Shibe.

00:15:26.650 --> 00:15:28.360
<b>Third Period</b>

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:31.150
<b>blah blah</b>

00:15:28.640 --> 00:15:31.630
And the results of the third submissions...

00:15:28.740 --> 00:15:31.200
<b>this is lame, talk shit about someone!</b>

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.240
<b>will something finally happen?</b>

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:35.240
One card is not blank!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.110
That was faster than I expected.

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:39.500
I hope it's a really huge exposé!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.560
Even a small one is good at first.

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:43.300
While it might look trivial 
from the outside,

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:48.380
